# COPIED-METHOD-DECLARED-FORMAL, a nonidentity correspondence through a copied method's declared formal: b1\getm(c)
# admits c, a Cand {pad; x; x}, to getm's formal of Model {x} in the copy's space; the ordinal `[0]x` reads Cand's
# first x (1) and the bare `x` -- the LAST occurrence -- its last x (9).  19.  Exit 7; 81 otherwise.
Model:
    int: x 0
end: Model
Cand:
    int: pad 5
    int: x 1
    int: x 9
end: Cand
fn: getm (Model: q) int
    int: a 0
    int: b 0
    a: q\[0]x
    b: q\x
    return: a * 10 + b
end: getm
Box:
    int: v 0
    fn: getm
end: Box
b1: merge: Box
c: merge: Cand
int: r b1\getm(c)
int: ok 7
if: r != 19
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
